text: |-
  Showing results for United States
  Utah's SB0082, the Autopsy Photo Amendments bill,
  was signed into law on March 26, 2025, and became
  effective on May 7, 2025. 2 The law criminalizes
  the knowing sharing, publication, or distribution of
  autopsy photographs that are part of a medical
  examiner's record, classifying it as a class B
  misdemeanor unless the photo is in the public
  domain. 1 The legislation establishes strict rules for
  the release of medical examiner records, including
  autopsy reports and photographs, limiting access to
  immediate relatives, legal representatives,
  physicians, law enforcement, and researchers under
  specific conditions.
  2
  • The bill amends Utah Code Section 26B-8-217 to
  enhance the confidentiality of medical examiner
  records, particularly photographs from
  autopsies. 1
  • It defines "deidentify" as removing personally
  identifying information about a decedent or their
  family. 3
  • Access to records is permitted for research
  purposes only if the researcher has an advanced
